# SwiftFormat configuration for OpenSheets.
#
# The point of pinning this is that eleven agents write code into one repository and the diffs
# have to be about behaviour, not about whether someone's editor reflowed a file. CI runs
# `--lint`, so a violation is a build failure rather than a review comment.
#
# Pinned to a version so an upgrade is a deliberate commit and not a surprise red build.
--swiftversion 6.0

# 110 rather than 100: this codebase carries long doc comments and descriptive type names, and
# a tighter limit turns readable signatures into ragged wrapped ones.
--maxwidth 120

--indent 4
--tabwidth 4
--linebreaks lf
--semicolons never
--commas always
--trimwhitespace always
--emptybraces no-space
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections preserve
--wrapreturntype preserve
--wrapconditions preserve
--closingparen balanced
--funcattributes preserve
--typeattributes preserve
--varattributes preserve
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--importgrouping alpha
--patternlet hoist
--elseposition same-line
--guardelse auto
--header ignore
# Spaced ranges: `0 ..< count`, not `0..<count`. Both are legible; this one is what the
# codebase already reads like, and picking the other would rewrite every bounds check for no gain.
--ranges spaced
--operatorfunc spaced
--shortoptionals always
--someany true
--extensionacl on-declarations
--redundanttype inferred
--voidtype void

# Group from five digits up. Grouping at four would turn every year literal in the date tests
# into `2_023`, which is worse than the thing grouping is meant to fix.
--decimalgrouping 3,5
--hexgrouping 4,8
--binarygrouping 4,8
--octalgrouping 4,8
--exponentgrouping disabled
--fractiongrouping disabled

# Rules we deliberately turn off.
#
# `blankLinesAroundMark` and `organizeDeclarations` fight the `// MARK:` layout used throughout
# `SheetModel`, where marks group a type's API by role rather than by declaration kind.
#
# `sortedSwitchCases` would reorder `SheetError`, whose case order is documentation: cases are
# grouped by subsystem in the order a file is processed.
#
# `wrapMultilineStatementBraces` and `blankLineAfterSwitchCase` add churn without adding clarity.
# `wrapEnumCases` would put `case none, thin, medium, thick` on four lines. For a closed set of
# style tokens the compact form is the readable one.
#
# `hoistTry` rewrites `#expect(try foo() == bar)` into `try #expect(foo() == bar)`, which reads
# as though the expectation throws rather than the call inside it.
--disable organizeDeclarations, sortedSwitchCases, wrapMultilineStatementBraces, blankLineAfterSwitchCase, docComments, wrapEnumCases, hoistTry, hoistAwait

# Rules we explicitly want, beyond the defaults.
--enable isEmpty, redundantParens, redundantReturn, redundantSelf, sortImports, blankLinesAtStartOfScope, blankLinesAtEndOfScope

--exclude .build,Packages/**/.build,Fixtures,Scripts/.venv,DerivedData,build
